   "detail": "Tested twice and failed twice. Stripping the jump component out of the Yang-Zhang sigma: -0.24%/+0.26%/-0.16% OOS QLIKE against a +2% bar. Feeding the continuous and jump components in as separate HAR regressors (the form built to carry exactly this): +0.4% to -0.7% against the same HAR without the split. This is why the page describes today and claims nothing about tomorrow."
